{
  "scope": "Embodied agent harnesses: frontier LLMs / VLMs (including coding agents) wrapped in a harness — interface and action calls, perception and control primitives as tools, frozen VLAs / skills / learned policies as tools, memory, verification and feedback, execution control — to control embodied systems (manipulation, navigation / VLN, aerial vehicles, humanoids, mobile manipulation) in simulation or the real world; training compact VLM / VLA students from harness or teacher trajectories (SFT, on-policy distillation, DAgger-style correction); RL inside the harness; harness self-optimisation in embodied settings; and evaluation methodology for these systems. Pure VLA policies with no harness or agent loop, GUI / computer-use agents, non-embodied harness self-improvement, and wire or test harnesses are out of scope.",

